<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile sells 1.1 million pounds of cobalt.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile sells 1.1 million pounds of cobalt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Defense National Stockpile Center said it sold about 1.1 million pounds of cobalt for an estimated provisional value of $18 million to seven companies.</p>
<p>The winners in the negotiated bid process were OMG Americas, Phoenixx International Resources, The Hall Chemical Company, Voss Metals Co, Glencore Limited, The Shepherd Chemical Co, and S. Wilkoff &amp; Sons Co.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
